1. Overview & Key Concepts

Service Request: A formal request from a user for something to be provided, added, moved, or changed (e.g., hardware, software access, standard IT services).

Request Fulfillment: The process of managing the lifecycle of all service requests from submission to closure.

Objective: Ensure service requests are processed efficiently, accurately, and through predefined standard workflows.

2. Request Data Structure & Hierarchy

Request Management in ServiceNow follows a three-level hierarchy:

[ REQ ] Request (Header / Order Number)
   │
   └── [ RITM ] Requested Item (Specific Item/Service Requested)
          │
          └── [ SCTASK ] Service Catalog Task (Operational Execution Steps)


Request (REQ): The parent record representing the overall order placed by the user.

Requested Item (RITM): The specific catalog item or service selected (a single Request can contain multiple RITMs).

Service Catalog Task (SCTASK): The discrete work assignment(s) created for fulfillment teams (Fulfillers) to execute the request.

3. End-to-End Request Lifecycle

[ User Submits Request ] ──► [ Approval Workflow ] ──► [ Task Assignment ] ──► [ Execution & Closure ]


Step 1: Request Submission

Users navigate to the Self-Service Portal / Service Catalog.

Users select the required item/service, fill in necessary parameters, and submit the request.

Step 2: Approvals (If Applicable)

If the item requires managerial or financial approval, system notifications are automatically dispatched to the designated approver.

The request remains in Pending Approval state until approved.

If rejected, the request is canceled automatically, and the requester is notified.

Step 3: Task Assignment & Fulfillment

Upon approval, the system triggers the predefined workflow and generates one or more Catalog Tasks (SCTASK).

Tasks are assigned to the respective Fulfiller Group.

Fulfillers access their queue via Service Desk > My Groups Work or Work Overview.

Fulfillers update task status (In Progress, Work Notes, etc.) during execution.

Step 4: Resolution & Auto-Closure

When all associated Catalog Tasks (SCTASK) are marked as Closed Complete, the parent Requested Item (RITM) and Request (REQ) are automatically updated to Closed Complete.

4. Fulfiller Best Practices

Work Notes vs. Additional Comments: Use Work Notes for internal technical updates visible only to IT staff. Use Additional Comments to communicate directly with the end-user.

Timely Updates: Always move tasks to In Progress when work begins to maintain accurate metrics and SLA tracking.

Task Closure: Ensure all prerequisites and verifications are completed before closing a task.
